@*
    The scope caption: what the figures beneath it actually cover.

    A degraded scope is rendered as an alert, not as an aside. The facade fails
    closed - an AllTenants request it cannot validate is served as one tenant
    instead of refused - so the only thing standing between an operator and
    reading one tenant's traffic as the whole cluster's is this line. That makes
    it a correctness surface, which is why the degraded branch uses role="alert"
    and the ordinary branch role="status".

    Nothing here is computed. The caption arrived already composed from the scope
    the facade reported, so this component renders a string and picks a class.
*@

@if (Caption.Text is { Length: > 0 })
{
    @if (Caption.IsDegraded)
    {
        <p class="lxt-scope is-warn" role="alert">
            <strong class="lxt-scope-lead">Narrower than you asked for.</strong>
            @Caption.Text
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="lxt-scope" role="status">@Caption.Text</p>
    }
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The caption to render, composed from the scope the facade pinned.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public TelemetryScopeCaption Caption { get; set; }
}
